From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:06:20 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132: Add the CPU capacities

Without capacity-dmips-mhz the scheduler sees the E and P cores as
equal, so it places heavy tasks on E cores as readily as on P cores.

The E core value is measured on the J713. Eight workloads (xz, zstd,
gzip, bzip2, sha256sum, b2sum and a perl and an awk loop) ran on an E
and a P core with the clusters held at 2.172 and 2.088 GHz, counting the
user cycles each needed for the same instructions. Per cycle an E core
does 0.50 to 0.95 of a P core's work, 0.662 as the geometric mean,
which is 677 against the P cores' 1024.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
index 8351a2430f44..d1c11bbe41a9 100644
